#!/usr/bin/env bash
# SessionStart hook: declare where the superpowers skills write their FILE artifacts for this
# repo, overriding the vendored docs/superpowers/ default with a gitignored .local/ root.
# Tier-independent. Offline-safe: no network, no repo reads.
set -euo pipefail

# Raw text -> JSON additionalContext (Claude Code hook shape). printf, not heredoc
# (bash 5.3+ heredoc hang, see obra/superpowers#571).
emit() {
  local s="$1"
  s="${s//\\/\\\\}"; s="${s//\"/\\\"}"
  s="${s//$'\n'/\\n}"; s="${s//$'\r'/\\r}"; s="${s//$'\t'/\\t}"
  printf '{\n  "hookSpecificOutput": {\n    "hookEventName": "SessionStart",\n    "additionalContext": "%s"\n  }\n}\n' "$s"
}

emit "<superpowers-artifact-locations>
For this repo, the superpowers skills write their FILE artifacts under a gitignored,
machine-local root — NOT the upstream \`docs/superpowers/\` default. Treat the paths below as the
declared 'user preference' those skills defer to:

- Design specs (brainstorming): \`.local/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md\`
- Implementation plans (writing-plans): \`.local/superpowers/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature>.md\`

Before writing the first artifact, ensure \`.local/\` is gitignored: if \`git check-ignore -q .local\`
fails, add a \`.local/\` line to \`.gitignore\` and commit it. Do NOT commit anything under \`.local/\`.

Worktrees are unaffected — keep them at superpowers' own \`.worktrees/\` default (it self-ignores
and self-cleans). Do not move worktrees under \`.local/\`.
</superpowers-artifact-locations>"
exit 0
